cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or code, please cite it as below."
title: "Continual Learning Bibliometrics: who moved continual learning to LLMs"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Arthur
    family-names: Fachel
    affiliation: "Pontifícia Universidade Católica do Rio Grande do Sul (PUCRS)"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-9903-6590"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ArthurFachel/cl-bibliometrics"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible bibliometric study of continual learning and catastrophic
  forgetting research, built from an OpenAlex snapshot of 2026-10-19
  (9,326 focused works). It measures growth, sub-areas, countries and
  institutions, benchmark migration, and who drove the shift to LLMs and
  pre-trained models, with every rule validated against three LLM labellers
  on held-out samples.
keywords:
  - continual learning
  - catastrophic forgetting
  - bibliometrics
  - scientometrics
  - OpenAlex
  - large language models
license: MIT
version: 1.0.1
date-released: "2026-10-21"
